orization. So commit.\n\nLet's ensure JSON valid. If arguments_json is JSON-encoded string, we need escape quotes inside. So output as:\n{\n  \"kind\": \"tool\",\n  \"tool\": \"commit\",\n  \"arguments_json\": \"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a1\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":1233,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"commit-P2F-FORMAL-L-010-quantity-a1\\\"}\",\n  \"report_json\": \"{}\"\n}\n\nThat's exactly one JSON object. Good.","signature":"86cdbc25-06c8-40c0-8a36-606d04c9bd76"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"commit\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a1\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":1233,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"commit-P2F-FORMAL-L-010-quantity-a1\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":1792,"output_tokens":997,"service_tier":"standard"}}